Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: Wait for VM clears before enabling CPU updates

The initial root page-table clear is submitted through SDMA and recorded
as a BOOKKEEP fence. amdgpu_bo_sync_wait only examines READ and lower
reservation usages. It therefore misses that clear when make_compute
switches to CPU updates. A delayed SDMA clear can erase the CWSR mapping
that KFD has just written, causing gfx1201 trap instruction-fetch faults.

Wait for all root reservation usages at this transition. Keep the wait
interruptible and retain its long result until checking for an error.
Limit the new wait to the first transition from SDMA to CPU updates,
under the root reservation. Retries and racing acquires can already carry
an unsignaled KFD eviction fence after CPU updates were enabled. Preserve
the existing implicit wait on every CPU-mapping path. Broadening the
shared implicit-sync helper would affect unrelated paths.

Target: amdgpu DKMS 6.19.14-2364437.24.04, amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vm.c
Base SHA256: dc2cfcf5c11b86dc16247dce712fe826c7de672cd27f8d3759cb7ca0a1a9d1e5
---
--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vm.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_vm.c
@@ -2720,7 +2720,24 @@
 		  "CPU update of VM recommended only for large BAR system\n");
 
 	if (vm->use_cpu_for_update) {
-		/* Sync with last SDMA update/clear before switching to CPU */
+		/* Initial SDMA clears use BOOKKEEP fences, which implicit
+		 * synchronization excludes. Once CPU updates are enabled,
+		 * retries can carry KFD eviction fences and must not wait
+		 * for all BOOKKEEP users again.
+		 */
+		if (vm->update_funcs != &amdgpu_vm_cpu_funcs) {
+			long wait_ret;
+
+			wait_ret = dma_resv_wait_timeout(
+				amdkcl_ttm_resvp(&vm->root.bo->tbo),
+				DMA_RESV_USAGE_BOOKKEEP, true, MAX_SCHEDULE_TIMEOUT);
+			if (wait_ret < 0) {
+				r = wait_ret;
+				goto unreserve_bo;
+			}
+		}
+
+		/* Keep implicit synchronization for existing CPU VMs too. */
 		r = amdgpu_bo_sync_wait(vm->root.bo,
 					AMDGPU_FENCE_OWNER_UNDEFINED, true);
 		if (r)
